On Fri, Feb 6, 2015 at 2:12 PM, Joseph Flanagan <jflan...@gmail.com> wrote:
> df %>%
>     group_by(lemma) %>%
>     summarise_each(funs(sum), n, total_words) %>%
>     mutate(percentage = n / total_words)

Unless I'm mistaken, you simply need to group by person too.

df %>%
    group_by(lemma, person) %>%

    summarise_each(funs(sum), n, total_words) %>%
    mutate(percentage = n / total_words)

