MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If I understand your problem, it is that you have a set of identical transformation steps you want to do for two identically structured but different datasets, and you don’t want to have to copy and paste code which comes with possibilities of error, maintenance costs, etc.  This sounds to me exactly what functions are for.  So define a function that takes an appropriately shaped dataset and outputs the result you want, then you can use that one-liner as many times as you want.   In this case, it doesn’t matter whether you use dplyr or anything else inside the function, so long as it takes data of structure X and returns data of structure Y.

PE

